<!--
  User-facing text.

  Most of the app's text is still written inline in Kotlin. This file is the
  start of moving it out, not the finished job: `node scripts/find-hardcoded-strings.mjs`
  reports what is left, so the size of the remaining work is a number somebody
  can look at rather than a guess.

  Before adding a language, read TRANSLATING.md. The short version: the terms
  that matter most here are statutory — gratuity, professional tax, perquisite,
  Chapter VI-A, compensatory off — and a plausible-sounding wrong word tells an
  employee their legal entitlement incorrectly, in a way neither they nor we can
  spot. Those must come from somebody who knows both the language and Indian
  payroll, never from a machine.
-->
